%% One valuation run, in order, with the real operations named.
%% Note: avoid "->" and angle brackets inside message text; mermaid's sequence
%% lexer reads them as arrow tokens and fails to parse.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant MD as market_data.json
  participant B as bootstrap_module
  participant QL as QuantLib GlobalBootstrap
  participant SC as spline_coeffs
  participant GPU as CUDA device
  participant V as reconciliation

  MD->>B: 8 curves, quotes tagged (rate, tenor, instrument)

  loop per curve, in dependency order
    B->>B: map each quote to its RateHelper
    alt meeting-dated or IMM-dated
      B->>QL: stage 1, strip only: ForwardRate + BackwardFlat
      QL-->>B: flat forwards, jumps only on policy or IMM dates
      B->>B: freeze strip zeros as ZeroPinHelper
      B->>QL: stage 2: pins plus long instruments
      QL-->>B: StepSplineCurve composite, split at tCut
    else single stage
      B->>QL: Discount trait, LogCubic interpolator
      QL-->>B: term structure
    end
    Note over QL: all n pillars solved simultaneously.<br/>A global interpolator has no<br/>bracketing sequential solve.
  end

  B->>SC: calibrated term structures
  loop per pillar interval
    SC->>SC: sample logDF at x0, x0+h/3, x0+2h/3, x1
    SC->>SC: Newton divided differences yield c0..c3
  end
  SC->>GPU: cudaMemcpy CubicCoeffs [c0..c3, xL, xR, form]
  Note over SC,GPU: the curve IS piecewise cubic in logDF,<br/>so this upload is an identity, not a fit

  par CPU reference path
    B->>V: prices and market PV01, re-bootstrapped per quote bump
  and GPU path
    GPU->>GPU: binary search interval, then Horner
    GPU->>V: device prices and pillar ladder
  end

  V->>V: difference both paths over 240 instruments
  V-->>MD: worst agreement 3.6e-14
